PASS: quote-driftwood: implied loss ratio 22.8571 (band 5.00-50.00, from the carrier's own signed terms, which declare max 50.0, min 5.0). 22.8571 = layer 2592075.49 / premium 113403.30, and identically 1 / (rate 0.0350 x (1 + load 0.2500)) = 22.8571. The numerator is the insured's ORDINAL exposure inside the layer, not an expected layer loss -- the insured signs a point total and no distribution exists to take one from -- so this is the reciprocal of the rate on line and NOT an actuarial loss ratio. It becomes one at formula 2.0.0, when the exposure section carries {ale, var95, tvar, tail} and the premium is priced as (1 + load) x E[loss in layer].
